        "original_id": "ac9d3b66-1c15-5839-a86b-9a5d96f38220",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lüliang, Shanxi, China, Shaanxi, Yellow River, Jinzhong, Taiyuan, Linfen, Xinzhou, Fuxin, Zhongyang County\n- Topics: geography, population, administrative divisions\n\nFacts:\n- Lüliang is a prefecture-level city in western Shanxi province, China.\n- Lüliang borders Shaanxi across the Yellow River to the west, Jinzhong and Taiyuan to the east, Linfen to the south, and Xinzhou to the north.\n- Lüliang has a total area of 21,143 km2.\n- Lüliang has a total population of 3,727,057.\n- At the 2010 census, the Lüliang metro area had a population of 320,142.\n- At the 2010 census, the prefecture of Fuxin had a total population of 1,819,339.\n- At the 2010 census, 669,317 people in Fuxin lived in the built-up area formed by four urban districts collectively called Fuxin City.\n- Zhongyang County is under the administration of Lüliang city.",
